Documentation: Snowflake Git Integration Issue (Bitbucket Workspace Setup) 
1. Summary of the Issue 
We attempted to configure Snowflake Workspaces to connect to our Bitbucket repository. 
However, Snowflake is returning the following errors: 
• “object does not exist or operation cannot be performed” 
• “unexpected PROVIDERS” when running SHOW API PROVIDERS 
These errors indicate that our Snowflake account does not have the Git Integration 
feature (git_https_api provider) enabled. 
This feature is required to connect Snowflake Workspaces to any Git provider (GitHub, 
Bitbucket, etc.). 
2. Why This Problem Occurs 
Even though the Snowflake region AWS_US_EAST_1 supports Git Integrations, 
the feature is not automatically enabled for every account. 
To use Git-based Workspaces, Snowflake must enable the following provider: 
git_https_api 
This provider is required to create the API INTEGRATION: 
CREATE API INTEGRATION ... API_PROVIDER = git_https_api; 
If the provider isn’t activated, Snowflake blocks the operation. 
3. Evidence of the Issue 
When running: 
SHOW API PROVIDERS; 
We receive the error: 
“unexpected PROVIDERS” 
This confirms that the Git Integration provider is not enabled in our account. 
When creating API integration: 
CREATE OR REPLACE API INTEGRATION bitbucket_integration 
API_PROVIDER = git_https_api 
API_ALLOWED_PREFIXES = ('https://bitbucket.org/<workspace>/') 
ENABLED = TRUE; 
Snowflake returns: 
“object does not exist or operation cannot be performed” 
This is the expected failure when the Git provider is missing. 
4. Impact 
• We cannot connect Snowflake Workspaces to Bitbucket. 
• We cannot create Git repositories inside Snowflake. 
• Developers cannot use Workspaces for SQL/DBT version control. 
• Git-based CI/CD inside Snowflake is blocked. 
This stops our planned development workflow. 
5. Required Action 
We must raise a Snowflake Support ticket requesting activation of the Git Integration 
feature. 
This is a standard step and usually completed in 1–4 hours. 
6. Support Ticket Message (Copy/Paste Ready) 
Subject: Request to Enable git_https_api Provider for Git Integration 
Message: 
Hello Snowflake Support, 
We are trying to configure Snowflake Workspaces with a Bitbucket repository. 
However, we are unable to create an API INTEGRATION using the provider 
`git_https_api`. 
Running `SHOW API PROVIDERS` returns "unexpected PROVIDERS", which indicates 
that the Git Integration feature (git_https_api provider) is not enabled for 
our account. 
Could you please enable the Git Integration feature, including the 
`git_https_api` API provider, for our Snowflake account in region AWS_US_EAST_1? 
This is required for Git Repository integration and Workspace functionality. 
Thank you. 
7. What Happens After Support Enables It 
Once Snowflake activates the provider: 
✔ SHOW API PROVIDERS will work 
✔ git_https_api will appear in the list 
✔ The API INTEGRATION creation will succeed 
✔ We can create the Bitbucket Git Repository 
✔ Developers can use Snowflake Workspaces normally 
